Package: bfd
Architecture: all
Depends: bash (>= 4.1), coreutils, grep, mawk | gawk, findutils,
 util-linux, iproute2, sed, procps, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: cron, logrotate
Suggests: bsd-mailx | mailutils
Description: Brute Force Detection - modular shell-based brute force attack monitor
 BFD is a modular shell-based daemon that parses authentication logs and
 detects brute-force login attempts. It uses an exponential-decay pressure
 scoring model to distinguish real attacks from typos, and bans offending
 IPs via configurable firewall backends (APF, CSF, firewalld, UFW, nftables,
 iptables, or route blackhole).
 .
 BFD runs in watch mode (~10s detection) or via cron (~2m detection) and
 includes per-rule pressure weights, country-based multipliers, ban
 escalation, and email alerting.
